      "heading": "Turn findings into reviews",
      "html": "<p>An audit that ends in a filed report is half done. Each flagged plan needs a job, an owner and a date. Then someone must see it through.</p><p>Quickler makes each finding a To do. The manager sees which plans were flagged and whether the reviews happened. A regional lead sees every home at a glance, without reading a single plan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What does a care plan audit check?</h3><p>It samples care plans. Is each one current? Is it written around the person? Is there proof of consent? Where capacity is in doubt, was the right assessment done? It tests care planning, not the clinical detail of one plan.</p><h3>Does Quickler store care plans?</h3><p>No. It records only your finding: the plan was in order, or it was not. The plan stays in your care system.</p><h3>How many plans should we sample?</h3><p>There is no set number by law. Pick a sample, and rotate it so every plan is checked in time. Follow your own policy and your regulator's latest guidance.</p><h3>Can I do it in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Read each plan in your care system. Send your finding by text or voice note. Quickler writes the report and a review list. No new app. No login.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/cqc-compliance-audit-checklist-uk.html\">CQC compliance audit checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/safeguarding-audit-care-home-uk.html\">Safeguarding audit for care homes</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-checklist-monthly-uk.html\">Monthly care home compliance checklist</a></li></ul>"
